      ],
      [
        "Performance Features",
        "1. The investment is only 1/3‑1/5 of that of conventional production lines with the same processing capacity. The production cost per ton of sand and gravel is only 1/3‑1/4 of that of conventional production lines.\n2. High degree of production automation, with fewer than 3 production personnel per shift.\n3. Short investment payback period, generally recoverable within 3 months. The sand making production line features high automation, low operating cost, high crushing ratio, energy saving, large output, low pollution and easy maintenance. The produced manufactured sand meets national construction sand standards, with uniform particle size, good grain shape and reasonable gradation.",
        "",
        "",
        ""
      ],
      [
        "Working Principle",
        "It is composed of vibrating feeder, jaw crusher, sand making machine, vibrating screen and belt conveyor. Materials fall vertically from the upper part of the machine into the high‑speed rotating impeller. Under the action of high‑speed centrifugal force, they collide and crush at high speed with another part of materials distributed around the impeller in an umbrella shape. After mutual collision, the materials form a vortex between the impeller and the casing, and are crushed through multiple mutual impacts and friction. They are discharged directly from the lower part, forming a closed‑circuit multiple cycle. The required finished particle size is controlled by screening equipment.",
        "",
